  "steps": [
    "Heat the oil in a large deep skillet over medium heat. Cook the onion and bell pepper 4-5 min until softened, then add the garlic for 30 sec.",
    "Add the beef, salt, pepper, paprika and chili powder. Cook, breaking up the meat, 5-6 min until no pink remains (160°F).",
    "Stir in the tomato sauce, water or broth, and macaroni. Bring to a boil, then cover, lower to medium-low, and simmer 10-12 min, stirring every few minutes, until the pasta is tender. Add a splash of water if it dries out before the pasta is done.",
    "Stir in the spinach until wilted. Serve topped with Parmesan and red pepper flakes."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "2 servings, about 412 cal and 33g protein each. Using water instead of broth may need more salt.",
    "Zucchini or corn work in place of the bell pepper, and it scales up for a week of lunches in a bigger pot."
  ],
